   "title": "Adding and Subtracting Fractions with Unlike Denominators",
   "focus": "Finding a common denominator before adding or subtracting fractions",
   "minutes": 15,
   "steps": [
    {
     "minutes": 3,
     "teacher": "Show 1/2 + 1/4. Point out that the bottom numbers are different, so we cannot just add the tops and bottoms straight across.",
     "students": "Observe the problem and discuss why the denominators must match."
    },
    {
     "minutes": 4,
     "teacher": "Explain how to find a common denominator by listing multiples, converting 1/2 to 2/4.",
     "students": "Follow along and help find the common denominator for 1/2 and 1/4."
    },
    {
     "minutes": 4,
     "teacher": "Demonstrate adding the converted fractions: 2/4 + 1/4 = 3/4. Emphasize that the denominator stays the same.",
     "students": "Practice the steps on mini-whiteboards with a similar problem."
    },
    {
     "minutes": 4,
     "teacher": "Guide students through 3/5 - 1/10, showing how to change 3/5 into 6/10 before subtracting.",
     "students": "Solve the subtraction problem step-by-step in their notebooks."
    }
   ],
